# Line endings are decided HERE, not by each machine's core.autocrlf. Without this file the
# answer depends on whose clone it is, and the whole repo re-diffs the first time someone with a
# different setting saves a file.

# Everything text is LF in the index and LF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except the two kinds of file Windows itself reads. cmd.exe can misread a label or a goto in a
# batch file saved with LF endings, which is how a working mvnw.cmd becomes a broken one on a
# clone that sets core.autocrlf=false. Maven's own wrapper ships these as CRLF for this reason.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary — never converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
